  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which acts as a target of multiple entities, including Oblonganoside C, NCI-H1734, and Tyrosine-protein kinase Fer. These entities all converge on Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets MCF7-DOX. The high scores in the visible paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship between Oblonganoside C and MCF7-DOX, likely mediated through Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The presence of multiple target entities pointing to the same downstream effect (MCF7-DOX) indicates a potential mechanism of action that is not yet fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central mediator in the interaction between Oblonganoside C and MCF7-DOX, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this relationship.",
